       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg as written, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The dose is 5 times the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any guideline that supports it. At that dose the risk of profound hypotension and shock is high, and the effect would last a long time because amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum labeled dose. I can add a note such as \"Uptitrated per specialist; further escalation under review.\"\n- **Enter a different dose** that you choose within the labeled range.\n- **Help with the next step.** If standard dosing has failed, the usual approach is to add another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, thiazide-like diuretic, or beta-blocker, rather than escalating amlodipine. I can enter one of those if you give me the drug and dose.\n\nIf the specialist does want a dose above the labeled maximum, please get direct verification. That means a pharmacist review and a documented order from the specialist or attending, entered through your institution's process for non-standard doses. I can't make that call from here.\n\nLet me know which option you'd like."
      }
     ],
